    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="RetDoc1044400001">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 2</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>RACHAEL BORELLI IS THE MOTHER OF THE BOARD PRESIDENT, DUSTYN EVANS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 6</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A NONPROFIT CORPORATION WITH MEMBERS ELECTING ONE MEMBER OF THE GOVERNING BODY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 7A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE MEMBERS OF THE ORGANIZATION ELECT THE DIRECTOR OF MEMBERSHIP FOR A TWO-YEAR TERM. THE DIRECTOR OF MEMBERSHIP HAS THE SAME VOTING RIGHTS AS ANY OTHER BOARD MEMBER.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE COMPLETED DRAFT FORM 990 IS REVIEWED BY THE TREASURER, BOOKKEEPER, AND ALL MEMBERS OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS AT LEAST WEEK PRIOR TO THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS MEETING WHERE IT IS FORMALLY APPROVED FOR FILING.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>ALL BOARD MEMBERS SIGN A CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY ACKNOWLEDGEMENT WHEN JOINING THE BOARD AND ANNUALLY THEREAFTER. ALL CONTRACTS ARE AWARDED BY THE EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR AND SIGNED BY THE BOARD PRESIDENT, EACH OF WHOM REVIEWS THEM FOR POSSIBLE CONFLICTS PRIOR TO EXECUTION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE COMPENSATION OF KEY EMPLOYEES IS EVALUATED BY THE OFFICERS OF THE ORGANIZATION. THE DISCUSSION INCLUDES A REVIEW OF WHAT OTHER ARTS ORGANIZATIONS PAY FOR SIMILAR POSITIONS, THE EARNINGS OF THE PERSON UNDER CONSIDERATION, AND THE OVERALL REASONABLENESS OF THE COMPENSATION. PERFORMANCE EVALUATIONS FOR KEY EMPLOYEES ARE FACILITATED BY THE BOARD PRESIDENT WITH INPUT FROM ALL MEMBERS OF THE BOARD. THE BOARD PRESIDENT RECOMMENDS SALARY ADJUSTMENTS TO THE BOARD AND THE BOARD VOTES ON THEIR ACCEPTANCE DURING A FORMAL MEETING.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE GOVERNING DOCUMENTS, AND CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY ARE POSTED ON THE CHORUS WEBSITE, ALONG WITH A NOTICE THAT THEY ARE AVAILABLE FOR IN-PERSON INSPECTION UPON REQUEST. A STATEMENT ON THE ORGANIZATION'S WEBSITE STATES THAT THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS ARE AVAILABLE UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
